**How `Parse` recognises a new file marker:**

`Parse` delegates to `findFileMarker`, which scans the data by first using `bytes.Index` to quickly jump to lines beginning with `"\n-- "` (the `newlineMarker` constant). When it lands on a candidate line, it calls `isMarker` to verify the full format: the line must start with `"-- "`, end with `" --"`, and have at least the 6-byte marker overhead. The enclosed text (trimmed of surrounding whitespace) becomes the filename.

**Function that checks a single line:**

`isMarker(data []byte) (name string, after []byte)` at line 117. It returns the filename and the remaining data after the marker line if the input starts with a valid marker; otherwise it returns an empty name.

```go
func isMarker(data []byte) (name string, after []byte) {
    if !bytes.HasPrefix(data, marker) {       // "-- "
        return "", nil
    }
    // ... find newline, strip \r if present ...
    if !(bytes.HasSuffix(data, markerEnd) && len(data) >= len(marker)+len(markerEnd)) {
        return "", nil                         // must end with " --"
    }
    return strings.TrimSpace(string(data[len(marker) : len(data)-len(markerEnd)])), after
}
```

